<title>NORWAY: FORECAST-Orkla profits seen falling.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Orkla profits seen falling.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian branded goods conglomerate Orkla ASA is expected to post a pre-tax profit of 634 million crowns for the first four months, according to a consensus forecast by eight analysts polled by Reuters.</p>
<p>The pre-tax profit for the first four months of 1996 was 706 million crowns.</p>
<p>The Orkla share has risen sharply on the Oslo Stock Exchange in the past few months, but the analysts believed there was still potential for further gains. Five had a buy recommendation on the share, two said hold and one said sell.</p>
<p>A comparison with forecasts ahead of the annual 1996 result shows that analysts have raised their earnings per share (EPS) forecast for 1997 by nearly 2.5 percent. For the first four months, they saw EPS at 9.36 crowns.</p>
